course: dictionary
lesson: 6401
title: Words for soft sounds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A murmur is a soft, low sound that goes on and on, like a stream, the wind or bees humming. Murmur can also be a verb, meaning to say something very quietly. Context shows you which meaning is right.
explain: «Toad ... at intervals he faintly murmured "Poop-poop!"» The word faintly is a clue: Toad was speaking softly, so murmured means said very quietly. Try the swap check: put «said quietly» in place of murmured, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Murmur can also be a noun. «They paid without a murmur» means they paid without complaining, so a murmur here is a quiet complaint. Read the whole phrase and ask what the words around it are really about.
fact: Murmur as a verb means to say something very quietly.
fact: Murmur as a noun means a soft, low sound that goes on and on, such as water, wind or bees.
fact: «Without a murmur» means without complaining.
fact: «A murmur of agreement» means a soft sound of people agreeing together.
fact: In medicine, a heart murmur is an extra sound a doctor hears in the heartbeat, and many are harmless.
exercise: «Going South, with the rest of them,» he murmured, «Seawards first and then on shipboard.» What does murmured mean here? | *Said very quietly | Shouted with joy | Sang loudly | Wrote it down
exercise: Everyone praises Toad, but he only murmurs «Not at all!» What does murmurs suggest about how Toad speaks? | *He says it very quietly, as if he is modest | He writes a letter about it | He sings it happily | He shouts it to win the praise
exercise: «They paid without a murmur.» What does murmur mean in this phrase? | A soft sound of water | *A quiet complaint | A kind gift | A loud cheer
test: «A murmur of surprise ran round the room.» What does murmur mean here? | A sudden silence with no sound at all | *A soft sound of many voices reacting | A loud shout of anger | A loud bang from the door
test: «The river murmurs and the reeds whisper.» What does murmurs mean in The Wind in the Willows? | Turns into mist and rises | Flows fast and roars over stones | Freezes over in the winter | *Makes a soft, low sound that goes on and on
exam: In «The river murmurs and the reeds whisper», what does murmurs mean? | A sharp bump against the bank | A quick, loud splash | A long, cold silence | *A soft, low sound that goes on and on
